From: Instinct Agent <agent@instinct.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:10:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Player real blur: player as haze source, drawers and
 popups frost behind the switch

- PlayerHost.frostEnabled(): the Blur effects switch answered by the
  platform (Android: switch + SDK>=12), default false.
- FrostedPlayerFrame draws the whole player as one haze source
  (sourceState); NowPlayingScreen passes playerHaze. Overlays stay
  siblings of the source subtree, so panels never sample themselves.
- FrostMaterial in sharedUi holds the one frost recipe (24dp, tint 60
  dark / 55 light by container luminance, opaque fallback); the app
  module's SpoolFrost now delegates to it, no drift.
- PlayerDrawer, LyricsOffsetSheet, MixViewPopup and AudioPopupCard draw
  hazeEffect over the player's source while the switch is on and their
  solid fills when it is off. AudioPopupCard's solid stopgap is
  reverted now that a real source exists.
- The dormant LocalPlayerFrost snapshot machinery stays off.
